{
  "dom_id": "step-e3315",
  "name": "Example: Finding a Trigonometric Ratio",
  "problem": "Given that $x=0.3$ radians, what is $\\sin{x}$ rounded to $3$ decimal places?",
  "worked_solution": "Note the argument of the sine is given in radians. Using a calculator in \"radians\" mode, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\sin(0.3) = 0.295\\,520\\ldots \\approx 0.296\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
